This is a big update! Three major issues highlighted here with the full list below.
 - Fixed the cable disconnect/DHCP issue Chris identified.
 - Added XMODEM download support over the UART
 - CTCSS now independently enableable for local, General Purpose, and GPS modes.

CHANGES SINCE REV 0.08
=================================
* Added user settable GPS time offset (numeric and parametric), mainly for interop with older GPSes.
* Changed factory default for dial timing from general purpose to GPS-timed.
* Found/fixed a bug that was sending GPS packets with a "0" timestamp
* Made the challenge string a random number generated at boot (like the Voter) and not a user setting.
* Clarified Host/Client password descriptions (thanks Kevin)
* Reformatted GPS lat/long strings in status GPS to separate degrees from minutes (Dave request)
* Added reminder to program after download in update sequence
* Adjusted the "rxtest dev3k" deviation to the right value (it was a placeholder I never got back to)
* Fixed rssimode, rxtest and update help texts, they were out of date
* Cleaned up Sat Signal for status gps a bit, fewer blank lines.
* XMODEM download support! "update xmodem". Download only, not verify and UART only for now.
* Added "status version" for HW and SW versions, deleted "hwrev" from show as it is now redundant.
* CTCSS now independently enablable for local, GP and GPS modes
* renamed xuart command to utest with parameter ext|s2n to test either s2n or external UART
* Found bug that hung Ethernet on cable unplug. Now Re-run DHCP on cable reconnect.
* Rx LED now has two user-selectable modes, audio level and COR/CTCSS state.
